<%# THE ALL TAB, POST-CUTOVER (plan 3, task 4, decision 6).

    ONE money-flow bar, not two. The old pair was "Income Allocation" (earned, split into
    Budgeted / Savings Contrib / Remaining) and "Expense Sources" (spent, split into From Income /
    From Savings). Savings Contrib summed savings-typed ENTRIES and was $0.00 for everyone; "From
    Savings" was enveloped spending under a name that made funding an envelope and raiding a goal
    the same event. Strip both untruths out and the two bars are one fact — income, the two lanes
    the spending came out of, and what is left — so it is drawn once.

    ** THE LEGEND NAMES THE TWO LANES IN THE WORDS THE OTHER TAB HEADS THEM WITH (FINAL review —
    M-2). ** These two rows read "Out of available" / "Out of an envelope" and the Expenses tab's own
    section headings read "Out of Available" / "Out of an Envelope" — one pair of phrases in two
    casings, a tab apart, on one screen. THE CAPITAL IS THE ONE THAT SURVIVES, on both halves: this
    is a LABEL beside a swatch rather than a sentence, and Reports Title-Cases every label it has
    ("Money Flow", "Health Indicators", "Tracked Available Spending"). The lowercase register is
    still the right one INSIDE a sentence — `_expenses_tab`'s "No spending out of available" is
    Budget's own convention ("Left over → available") and stays exactly as it is.

    `:all_v12` — the cache key's version, bumped so nothing rendered under the old shape survives
    (v11 was the legend's noun: "out of the buffer" became "out of available", spec §3; v12 is its
    casing).
%>
<% cache [current_user, selected_date, current_period, :all_v12] do %>
<% income = @presenter.total_tracked_income %>
<% expenses = @presenter.total_tracked_expenses %>
<% buffer_spending = @presenter.total_tracked_buffer_expenses %>
<% envelope_spending = @presenter.total_tracked_envelope_expenses %>
<% remaining = @presenter.net_amount %>

<div class="mb-8">
  <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-gray-900 mb-4">Money Flow</h3>

  <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded p-4">
    <h4 class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 mb-3">Where your income went</h4>
    <% if income.positive? %>
      <% denom = [income, expenses].max.to_f %>
      <% buffer_pct = (buffer_spending / denom * 100).round(1) %>
      <% envelope_pct = (envelope_spending / denom * 100).round(1) %>
      <% remaining_pct = [100 - buffer_pct - envelope_pct, 0].max.round(1) %>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
        <span class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-900"><%= number_to_currency(income) %> earned</span>
        <span class="text-sm font-medium <%= remaining >= 0 ? "text-brand-dark" : "text-terracotta" %>"><%= number_to_currency(remaining) %> left over</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex w-full h-8 rounded overflow-hidden">
        <% if buffer_pct.positive? %>
          <div class="bg-terracotta flex items-center justify-center" style="width: <%= buffer_pct %>%">
            <% if buffer_pct > 10 %>
              <span class="text-xs font-medium text-white"><%= buffer_pct %>%</span>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
        <% if envelope_pct.positive? %>
          <div class="bg-dusty-teal flex items-center justify-center" style="width: <%= envelope_pct %>%">
            <% if envelope_pct > 10 %>
              <span class="text-xs font-medium text-white"><%= envelope_pct %>%</span>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
        <% if remaining_pct.positive? %>
          <div class="bg-brand-dark flex items-center justify-center" style="width: <%= remaining_pct %>%">
            <% if remaining_pct > 10 %>
              <span class="text-xs font-medium text-white"><%= remaining_pct %>%</span>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-3 text-xs">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-terracotta"></span>
          <span class="text-gray-600">Out of Available <%= number_to_currency(buffer_spending) %></span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-dusty-teal"></span>
          <span class="text-gray-600">Out of an Envelope <%= number_to_currency(envelope_spending) %></span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-brand-dark"></span>
          <span class="text-gray-600">Left over <%= number_to_currency([remaining, 0].max) %></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% elsif expenses.positive? %>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-2">No income recorded <%= period_time_label %></p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">Spent: <%= number_to_currency(expenses) %></p>
    <% else %>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-center py-4">No data available <%= period_time_label %></p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>

<%# Health Indicators. "Budget Used" stood here and is deleted with the cap it measured — see
    Dashboard::OverviewPresenter for why the funded-vs-spent replacement is not built here, and
    "Net Savings" for why contributions-minus-withdrawals is not a figure this data supports. %>
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-8">
  <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded p-4">
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Spent</p>
    <p class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-700"><%= number_to_currency(expenses) %></p>
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">tracked spending <%= period_time_label %></p>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded p-4">
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Expense Ratio</p>
    <p class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-700"><%= @presenter.expense_ratio %>%</p>
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">of income spent</p>
  </div>
</div>

<%# Savings Pools Progress %>
<%= render "dashboard/savings_strip" %>

<%# Top Spending %>
<% top_categories = @presenter.top_expense_categories %>
<% if top_categories.any? %>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-gray-900 mb-4">Top Spending</h3>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <% top_categories.each do |cat| %>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between py-2 border-b border-gray-100">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <%= link_to cat[:name], category_path(cat[:id]), class: "text-gray-700 hover:text-brand-dark" %>
            <% if expenses.positive? %>
              <span class="text-xs text-gray-400"><%= (cat[:amount] / expenses.to_f * 100).round %>%</span>
            <% end %>
          </div>
          <span class="font-medium text-gray-900"><%= number_to_currency(cat[:amount]) %></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
<% end %>
